---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<SiteLayout current="practice" title="Tools: the real source of agent capability">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Agent capability</p>
      <h1>Tools: the real source of agent capability</h1>
      <p>
        A tool is any controlled interface that lets the model read fresh state
        or change the outside world. Different tool forms create different
        capability boundaries.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-directory">
      <a class="tool-row" href={url('/function-tools/')}>
        <div class="tool-row__kicker">Typed action</div>
        <div class="tool-row__content">
          <h3>Function tools</h3>
          <p>Small, explicit functions with schemas. Best for narrow actions like creating a ticket, validating an order, or checking machine status.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-row__arrow">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14m-7-7 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
      </a>
      
      <a class="tool-row" href={url('/mcp-servers/')}>
        <div class="tool-row__kicker">Shared interface</div>
        <div class="tool-row__content">
          <h3>MCP servers</h3>
          <p>External capability providers that expose tools, resources, and prompts. Useful when integrations need auth, state, or reuse across agents.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-row__arrow">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14m-7-7 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a class="tool-row" href={url('/skills/')}>
        <div class="tool-row__kicker">Packaged playbook</div>
        <div class="tool-row__content">
          <h3>Skills</h3>
          <p>Repeatable playbooks with instructions, scripts, templates, and examples. Good for domain workflows that need consistent execution.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-row__arrow">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14m-7-7 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a class="tool-row" href={url('/code-execution/')}>
        <div class="tool-row__kicker">Runtime feedback</div>
        <div class="tool-row__content">
          <h3>Code execution</h3>
          <p>A sandbox for calculating, transforming files, running tests, and inspecting repos. Powerful because observations are concrete.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-row__arrow">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14m-7-7 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a class="tool-row" href={url('/search-retrieval/')}>
        <div class="tool-row__kicker">Grounding</div>
        <div class="tool-row__content">
          <h3>Search and retrieval</h3>
          <p>Web search, docs lookup, vector search, and database queries. These tools keep decisions tied to current or private information.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-row__arrow">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14m-7-7 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a class="tool-row" href={url('/human-handoff/')}>
        <div class="tool-row__kicker">Control point</div>
        <div class="tool-row__content">
          <h3>Human handoff</h3>
          <p>Approval and review are control points too. In ADK, confirmation gates exist today, while longer-running workflow pauses are still part of the 2.0 beta.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-row__arrow">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14m-7-7 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a class="tool-row" href={url('/file-system-os/')}>
        <div class="tool-row__kicker">Local environment</div>
        <div class="tool-row__content">
          <h3>File system & OS</h3>
          <p>Tools for reading, writing, grepping, and navigating local directories. Essential for coding agents to manipulate the codebase and environment directly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-row__arrow">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14m-7-7 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a class="tool-row" href={url('/browser-computer-use/')}>
        <div class="tool-row__kicker">UI automation</div>
        <div class="tool-row__content">
          <h3>Browser & computer use</h3>
          <p>Interact with graphical UIs and control web browsers. <em>Note: We won't cover these in detail here as they are still relatively new and niche in general agentic development.</em></p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-row__arrow">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14m-7-7 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
